# `dangerous` bake-in.  The profile itself attenuates nothing: every
# field defaults to the lattice top (None / unset).  Use only when
# something else is the trust boundary (e.g. a Docker container).
#
# Exarch still layers its own exclusions on top: its binary is never
# runnable, its credential files are denied once some layer restricts
# the filesystem, and every `--restrict` file is denied.
#
# Combine with `--restrict <FILE>` to "start permissive and
# attenuate from there": the file, less those exclusions.

return ()
